

### Numerical Methods

#### 8.15 Use and Extension of the Tables Computation of \(P_{n}(z)\)

For all values of \(x\) there is very little loss of significant figures (except at zeros) in using the recurrence relation **8.5.3** for increasing values of \(n\). Example 1. Compute \(P_{n}(x)\) for \(x=.31415\)\(92654\) and \(x=2.6\) for \(n=2(1)8\).

